<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Other ratios from one ratio in a quadrant</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Given that \({@gname@}\,x = {@giv@}\) and \({@intv@}\), find the exact value of</p><div>(a) \({@oname@}\,x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) \(\tan x =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Use \(\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x = 1\): \({@oname@}^2 x = 1 - \left({@giv@}\right)^2 = {@sqoth@}\), so \({@oname@}\,x = \pm\sqrt{{@sqoth@}} = \pm {@abs(oth)@}\).</p><p>For \({@intv@}\), \(x\) is in the {@qword@} quadrant, where \({@oname@}\,x\) is {@osign@}. So \({@oname@}\,x = {@oth@}\).</p><p>(b) \(\tan x = \dfrac{\sin x}{\cos x} = {@tv@}\), which is {@tsign@} in the {@qword@} quadrant.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: the other ratios from one given ratio in a quadrant; any ratio given, three quadrants. Entry: opposite, adjacent, hypotenuse, 1 if sin is given else cos, quadrant. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 2, Chapter 7, Example 8, E1 and Exercise E, Q1. */
P: [[33,56,65,0,2],[12,5,13,1,3],[15,8,17,0,4],[24,7,25,1,2],[21,20,29,0,3],[9,40,41,1,4],[12,35,37,0,2],[28,45,53,1,3],[12,5,13,0,4],[15,8,17,1,2]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
o: P[ix][1]; a: P[ix][2]; h: P[ix][3]; gs: P[ix][4]; qd: P[ix][5];
qword: if qd = 2 then "second" elseif qd = 3 then "third" else "fourth";
intv: if qd = 2 then "90^\\circ \\lt x \\lt 180^\\circ" elseif qd = 3 then "180^\\circ \\lt x \\lt 270^\\circ" else "270^\\circ \\lt x \\lt 360^\\circ";
ss: if qd = 2 then 1 else -1; cs: if qd = 4 then 1 else -1;
sv: ss*o/h; cv: cs*a/h; tv: sv/cv;
giv: if gs = 1 then sv else cv; oth: if gs = 1 then cv else sv;
gname: if gs = 1 then "\\sin" else "\\cos"; oname: if gs = 1 then "\\cos" else "\\sin";
osign: if oth > 0 then "positive" else "negative"; tsign: if tv > 0 then "positive" else "negative";
negoth: -oth; sqoth: 1-giv^2; rectan: 1/tv; negtan: -tv;
ftv: if gs = 1 then giv/(oth+1) else (oth+1)/giv;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
