  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Trigonometry III: other ratios from one ratio</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.5: Given sin x or cos x and the quadrant, find the other ratio and tan x exactly using the Pythagorean identity.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Example 8, E1 and Question 1 in Exercise E of Chapter 7 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: either ratio given, three quadrants, new triples, randomised over a curated list, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
